## Context
DESIGN.md §2.8 gates, honoring R19-R21, R26/R27, and v1's Risk-3 soak — repo-
side work in this repo's Makefile and bench/, not upstream PRs. Target shape:
`check: lint figures fold-gate golden check-fast`; `check-slow: check rss-gate
convergence soak`.
- R19 fold gate: fold_sweep.mjs repointed at the tree under test; against
  stock upstream it is red BY CLASSIFICATION (recorded miss count), not by
  crash; waiver keyed to PR #19's URL, deleted on merge (0014).
- R21 golden gate, D11=set: pinned multilingual fixture corpus, ~40 queries,
  answer sets at k=10. Thresholds re-derived after the operator critique's F1
  kill (0013's legitimate minimum is 0.25, not above 0.5): mean Jaccard >=
  0.8; <= 5% of queries below 0.35; hard floor 0.2. Order deliberately
  ungated. Re-pins are commits whose set diff is the review artifact; re-pin
  at entry granularity when entries exist.
- R20 RSS gate: deterministic synthetic monster at 44,906,152 chars, entry-
  structured (~43k headings); assert worker VmHWM <= 500 MB, server p95 <=
  300 MB. Fixture informed by X3 (0025).
- R26/R27 convergence harness: fixture library, empty dataDir, 1 Hz status
  polls touching nothing else; asserts status <= 50 ms, monotone coverage,
  prefix arithmetic per stage at DESIGN.md §2.3's granularities; then
  edit-one-count-one and the identical-bytes resync with zero recompute (every
  `*.done` work delta 0; the touched items appear only as `resync.noop`
  verification, which the gate permits and nothing downstream of it) —
  the test that would have caught the shipped 92.7% defect. Phase 3 fixture:
  one quarantine, one monster, dateAdded ties.
- R13 soak: three P0s, full 10k drain, 1 query/s each, kill -9 the conductor
  twice; p95 <= 1.5 s, zero SQLITE_BUSY surfacing, WAL <= 256 MB, lease
  migration < 30 s, zero double-commits.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] fold gate in `make check`, red-by-classification against stock upstream, waiver documented
- [ ] golden gate with the re-derived thresholds and a committed pinned set
- [ ] rss gate asserting the ratified budgets against the synthetic monster
- [ ] convergence harness + soak specified as the RFC's acceptance spec now; runnable once its machinery and the mock local API exist (see amendments)
- [ ] fold/golden/RSS(pre-RFC form) in the Makefile with honest red/waiver states

## Amendments (implementation review, 2026-08-26)
The five gates sort into two piles, and the exit criteria read accordingly:
- BUILDABLE NOW: the fold gate (fold_sweep.mjs today always exits 0, prints a
  WARNING, and crashes on stock upstream by importing the absent
  normalizeForSearch — the gate needs the classification fallback, nonzero
  exit codes, and a writable built checkout, since none exists in-repo); the
  golden gate once 0029 delivers its fixture corpus; the RSS gate in its
  pre-RFC form — server-only against stock upstream, red-with-waiver (0011
  measured 2,084.9 MiB), the worker assertion joining post-RFC.
- THE RFC'S ACCEPTANCE SPEC: the convergence harness and the soak assert
  counters, prefix arithmetic, drift, pipeline:idle, lease migration, and
  double-commits — observables of a ledger and conductor that exist only once
  the RFC's machinery is BUILT (not merely filed). They are the executable
  spec the political review says to lead the upstream conversation with; they
  cannot run before the machinery exists, and they also need a mock Zotero
  local API (everything in bench/ talks to live Zotero) — an unticketed
  prerequisite (~2-3 days) that lands with them.
Also flagged (Copilot round 2): the rss-gate's slow-suite placement weakens
R20's letter ("asserted on every check"); the cadence question is now on
DECISIONS.md's awaiting-ratification list — build the gate either way, wire
it per the ruling.
